  "instructions": [
    "preheat the oven to 375\u00012f (190\u0000c).",
    "in a small bowl, whisk together lemon juice, olive oil, garlic, salt, black pepper, and korean chili flakes.",
    "sprinkle the reblochon cheese with thyme, rosemary, and parsley.",
    "place the cheese in a korean brass bowl and drizzle with the lemon juice mixture.",
    "add the chopped scallions, sliced red onion, and chopped fresh mint on top of the cheese.",
    "cover the bowl with aluminum foil and roast for 15 minutes.",
    "remove the foil and continue roasting for an additional 5-7 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.",
    "garnish with chopped fresh herbs and serve over korean brown rice.",
    "serve immediately and enjoy!",
    "reheat any leftovers in the oven at 375\u00012f (190\u0000c) for 5-7 minutes, or until warmed through.",
    "serve with additional chopped herbs and a side of steamed vegetables if desired.",
    "store leftovers in the refrigerator for up to 3 days or freeze for up to 2 months."
